{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared chat widget identity vectors (docs/SERVER_SDK_SPEC.md, Capability 6).",
    "",
    "`sign`: every signer (the Rails helper, devbench.WidgetIdentity in Go) must",
    "produce `token` exactly from secret, email, account, role, chat and issued_at.",
    "Inputs are given raw: the signer trims ASCII whitespace (space, TAB, LF, CR,",
    "FF, VT; nothing else) from email, account and role, then refuses invalid",
    "UTF-8 and any C0 control character or DEL left inside a field, then lowercases",
    "the email (U+0130 to a plain i), and de-duplicates and sorts `chat`.",
    "`chat`: null = no explicit permission (the tenant's settings decide);",
    "[] = this user may not chat; otherwise the user's capabilities.",
    "",
    "`refuse`: inputs a signer must refuse (no token, no widget) rather than sign.",
    "",
    "`verify`: what the chat service's verifier must conclude about `token` at",
    "`now` (Unix seconds) with `secret`. \"invalid\" covers forged, tampered,",
    "another tenant's secret, malformed and future-dated tokens; the service",
    "must not tell them apart. \"expired\" is reported only for a genuine token.",
    "",
    "Generated by internal/widgetid: go test ./internal/widgetid -update.",
    "Changing a vector breaks every signer in the field: new format, new prefix."
  ],
  "format": "dbw1.<base64url(issued_at \"\\n\" email \"\\n\" account \"\\n\" role \"\\n\" chat)>.<base64url(HMAC-SHA256(key=secret, \"dbw1.\" + payload))>; base64url unpadded; chat is \"\" (not stated), \"none\" (may not chat) or capabilities joined by \",\" in byte order",
  "capabilities": [
    "feature_requests",
    "handoff",
    "howto",
    "report",
    "status"
  ],
  "max_age_seconds": 86400,
  "max_future_skew_seconds": 300,
